.TH UPASFS 4
.SH NAME
upas/fs \- present a mailbox as a file system
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B upas/fs
[
.B -m
.I mountpt
]
.I mbox
.br
.B upas/fs -i
.B -u
.I user
.B -P
.I passfile
[
.B -s
.I server
] [
.B -a
.I dialip
] [
.B -n
.I n
] [
.B -m
.I mountpt
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Upas/fs
serves a mailbox as a file system, the Plan 9
.I upas
way, mounted at
.I mountpt
(default
.BR /mail/fs/mbox ).
Without
.B -i
it reads the Unix mbox file
.IR mbox .
With
.B -i
it instead fetches the most recent
.I n
messages (default 25) of the
.B INBOX
from an IMAP server over TLS (\c
.IR imap4 (2);
default Gmail), logging in as
.I user
with the app password in
.IR passfile ,
and serves those \(em so a live Gmail inbox is browsable with
.IR ls (1)
and
.IR cat (1).
As in
.IR upas-fetch (1),
.B -a
gives an already-resolved address to dial while the certificate is
verified for the
.B -s
name.
Each message becomes a numbered directory
.RB ( 1 ,
.BR 2 ,
\&...) so any program can read mail with
.IR ls (1)
and
.IR cat (1)
rather than parsing message syntax itself.
.PP
Within a message directory the read-only files are:
.TP
.B raw
the whole message as stored.
.TP
.B header
the header block (up to the first blank line).
.TP
.B body
the message body.
.TP
.B unixheader
the mbox
.B From_
envelope line.
.TP
.BR from ", " to ", " subject ", " date ", " cc ", " reply-to ", " message-id
the value of the corresponding header field, with continuation lines
folded; an absent field reads as empty.
.TP
.B type
the message's MIME content type.
.PP
A message is decomposed by MIME (see
.IR mime (2)).
.B body
is the decoded content \(em for a multipart message, its
.B text/plain
part.
A multipart message additionally contains a numbered subdirectory per
part
.RB ( 1 ,
.BR 2 ,
\&..., nested for nested multiparts), each with
.B type,
.B encoding,
a
.B filename
for an attachment, and the decoded
.BR body .
.PP
The server keeps running after it prints its start line; the mount lives
in the invoking name space.
.SH EXAMPLE
.EX

	upas/fs -m /mail/fs/mbox $home/mbox
	ls /mail/fs/mbox
	cat /mail/fs/mbox/1/subject

.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/upas/fs.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR upas-fetch (1),
.IR imap4 (2)
.SH BUGS
The mailbox is read (or fetched) once at start; it is not reread or
refreshed as it changes.
IMAP mode fetches whole messages up front rather than lazily.
